<title>UK: Berisford down, statement douses bid hopes.</title>
<headline>Berisford down, statement douses bid hopes.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Berisford Plc fell in early trading on Monday after the company said the possible bid approach it announced last week had come to nothing.</p>
<p>The stock was down 8-1/2p at 135-1/2 by 0802 GMT. Berisford said it was pleased that the uncertainty over the possible bid had ended and it could get on with its loan stock buyback programme.</p>
<p>The statement came after weekend press reports said the original bidder had pulled out, but said other bidders may be interested. The Mail on Sunday said Premark International of the U.S. could still mount a takeover bid.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 5106</p>
